2026-09-05  Fix upgrades with read-only Zsh caches

The installer skips generated .zwc and .zwc.old files when copying Oh My Zsh.
Existing caches and their permissions are preserved. Compiled caches are no longer
tracked or included in release archives. Rerun the one-line installer after a cache
permission failure; no manual permission changes are needed.

2026-09-05  Runtime reliability and maintenance

Shell startup uses cached version metadata and a background check with a daily interval.
Tool installers load on first use. Updates download one commit, verify a SHA-256 manifest
and shell syntax, preserve configuration symlinks, and save a snapshot for gcr rollback.
Failed writes and handled interrupts restore the previous contents.

New gcr status, doctor, install --dry-run and profile commands share a tool catalog.
User settings live in ~/.config/gcr/config.sh. Compose installers preserve existing
configuration and return deployment failures. Conda kernel registration uses the new
environment's Python. Terminal navigation supports both CSI and SS3 arrow sequences.

The runtime has focused modules, isolated Bash/Zsh regression tests and macOS/Ubuntu CI.
Existing installations must rerun sh install_gcr.sh once to install the new module layout.
See doc/runtime.md for configuration and recovery details.
